Basic Syntax
ansible-doc [options] <plugin_name>
1. View documentation for a module
ansible-doc ping

Example:

ansible-doc copy
ansible-doc file
ansible-doc service
ansible-doc apt
ansible-doc yum
2. List all available modules
ansible-doc -l

To search for a specific module:

ansible-doc -l | grep user

Output example:

ansible.builtin.user
community.general.htpasswd
3. Show examples only
ansible-doc -s copy

This displays a shortened version containing parameters and examples.

4. Show detailed documentation
ansible-doc file

This includes:

Description
Parameters
Examples
Return values
Notes
5. View documentation for collections
ansible-doc ansible.builtin.copy

or

ansible-doc community.general.htpasswd
6. List plugins by type
Connection plugins
ansible-doc -t connection -l
Inventory plugins
ansible-doc -t inventory -l
Callback plugins
ansible-doc -t callback -l
Lookup plugins
ansible-doc -t lookup -l
Become plugins
ansible-doc -t become -l
Cache plugins
ansible-doc -t cache -l
Filter plugins
ansible-doc -t filter -l
7. View documentation for a plugin

Example:

ansible-doc -t lookup file
ansible-doc -t connection ssh
8. Show all available plugin types
ansible-doc --help

Plugin types include:

module
inventory
lookup
connection
callback
strategy
shell
become
cache
filter
vars
test
9. Find a module

Suppose you want to find modules related to packages:

ansible-doc -l | grep package

or

ansible-doc -l | grep apt
10. Find modules for users
ansible-doc -l | grep user

Then inspect one:

ansible-doc user
Common Commands
Task	Command
List all modules	ansible-doc -l
View module documentation	ansible-doc copy
Short documentation	ansible-doc -s copy
List inventory plugins	ansible-doc -t inventory -l
List lookup plugins	ansible-doc -t lookup -l
List connection plugins	ansible-doc -t connection -l
View SSH connection plugin	ansible-doc -t connection ssh
Search for modules	ansible-doc -l | grep copy
View user module	ansible-doc user
Show help	ansible-doc --help
Practical Examples

Check the copy module:

ansible-doc copy

Check the service module:

ansible-doc service

Check the systemd module:

ansible-doc systemd

Check the template module:

ansible-doc template

Check the lineinfile module:

ansible-doc lineinfile

Check the apt module:

ansible-doc apt

Check the yum module:

ansible-doc yum

These commands are among the most useful during playbook development because they let you quickly verify a module's parameters, examples, and return values without leaving the terminal.
